  "worked_solution": "We find the derivative of $f(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(t) & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(3t)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t,\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,3{t}^{2}\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
